  "question": {
    "text": "A battery is connected between two points&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> on the circumference of a uniform conducting ring of radius&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math> and resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math>. One of the arcs&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>AB</mi></math> of the ring subtends an angle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">θ</mi></math> at the centre. The value of the magnetic induction at the centre due to the current in the ring is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "b3D6u",
      "text": "proportional to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>180</mn><mo>°</mo><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">θ</mi><mo>)</mo></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "TUUU8",
      "text": "inversely proportional to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "kwHXb",
      "text": "zero, only if&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>180</mn><mo>°</mo><mo>)</mo></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "A8Okq",
      "text": "zero for all values of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">θ</mi></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "For a current flowing into a circular arc, the magnetic induction at the centre is<br /><br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <math> <mrow> <mtext>B</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <mrow> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <msub> <mi>&#956;</mi> <mn>0</mn> </msub> <mi></mi><mi></mi><mi></mi><mi></mi><mi></mi><mi></mi><mi></mi><mi></mi><mi></mi><mi></mi><mi>i</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>4</mn> <mi>&#960;</mi> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </mfenced> <mi>&#160;&#952;</mi> </mrow> </mrow> </math><br /><br />or&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>B</mtext><mo>&#8733;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#952;</mi></math><br /><br />In the given problem, the total current is divided into two arcs<br /><br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mo>&#8733;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mtext>resistance of arc</mtext></mfrac></math><br /><br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<math> <mrow> <mo>&#8733;</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mtext>length of arc</mtext> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </math><br /><br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <math> <mrow> <mo>&#8733;</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mtext>angle subtended at centre&#160;</mtext> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mi>&#952;</mi> </mrow> </mfenced> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </math><br /><br /><br /><u><strong><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/EM0007049_AnsExp4_1.jpg\" style=\"width: 224px; height: 226px;\" /></strong></u><br /><br /><br />or&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>i</mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mtext>constant</mtext></math><br /><br />i.e., magnetic field at centre due to arc&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>AB</mi></math> is equal and opposite to the magnetic field at centre due to arc <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ACB</mi></math>. Or the net magnetic field at the centre is zero.",
